# --- [RETIRED 2026-08-29. These three globs were BROADER THAN THE INTENT, and
#     that is the exact failure this file's own header warns about.]
#
#     They read as "we skip these backends". The tree said otherwise: 168 of
#     170 ggml-opencl kernels, 49 of 51 webgpu shaders and 56 of 59 et-kernels
#     were vendored. The directories were never skipped — so what the globs
#     actually did was retroactively legitimize a handful of files that
#     arrived in the 035e22731a fast-forward and were never taken. Two OpenCL
#     kernels (moe_add_id_glu.cl, ssm_scan.cl), two WebGPU shaders and nine
#     ggml-et build inputs were missing, and the reverse pass reported a clean
#     tree because a declared omission is by definition not a discrepancy.
#
#     An exclusion whose premise is "we do not build that today" expires
#     silently the moment a host does. It expired twice: Metal on 2026-08-26
#     (PR #52 landed green from Linux, broke every Mac) and CUDA on
#     2026-08-28 (the container image is the first host in the fleet that
#     compiles it). Both were found by a machine that builds that backend,
#     after landing, never by a gate.
#
#     All 13 files are now vendored — 31 KB — and the globs are gone. THE RULE
#     THIS LEAVES: exclude by whether a file is a BUILD INPUT, never by which
#     backend the fleet happens to compile this month. A source, shader,
#     kernel, linker script or .cmake goes in the tree whether or not anything
#     switches it on.

# --- CUDA: NOW VENDORED (2026-08-28). This block used to exclude four files
